{
 "id": "459866fa-ce22-4e66-8958-4d180ccc6103",
 "name": "anchor: auth",
 "tags": [
  "anchor"
 ],
 "description": "Platform authentication end to end with a throwaway invited admin: register (invitation consumed), /v1/me, login, refresh, logout, the 400/401 cases with their codes (refresh 401s carry no body by contract, so they assert the cleared cookie), no password echoed, and a deleted user unable to log in. Logout revokes the session's refresh token. Refresh rotates the token: the rotated token keeps working, the original replayed after the 10s reuse grace is refused and revokes the whole session. Deleting the platform user revokes its sessions: a refresh token from a session still active at cleanup is refused afterwards.",
 "updated_at": "2026-11-03T15:14:19.49251Z",
